    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d241">

                <pb facs="0408" n="284" xml:id="pg284"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">824.00/176: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Ambassador in Argentina</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Stimson</hi>) <hi
                        rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of
                    State</hi></head>
                <opener><seg rendition="#center">[Paraphrase]</seg></opener>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Buenos Aires</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1921-02-02T13:00:00-04:00"><hi rendition="#italic">February 2,
                                1921—1 p.m.</hi></date><lb/>[Received 9:12 p.m.]</dateline></opener>
                <p>29. Your telegram no. 13, January 31, has been acted upon. I was informed by the
                    Under Secretary of Foreign Affairs that the recognition of Bolivia has already
                    been the subject of discussion between the Department and the Argentine
                    Ambassador in Washington. The Ambassador has been instructed to inform you that
                    his Government concurs fully in the decision taken by the Government of the
                    United States, and has suggested February 5th as the date to extend recognition
                    to the Bolivian Government. If, in the Department’s opinion, this date is too
                    early, the Argentine Government will gladly accept a later date.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Stimson</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
